  "_comment": "Context-aware confusable corrections. A valid word (that the engine would otherwise never touch) is rewritten to its contraction ONLY when the immediately-following word — typed a moment later — is in that entry's trigger set. Deliberately conservative: triggers are restricted to followers where the plain word is essentially never grammatical (a noun/adjective/3rd-person-verb before a bare verb, or a possessive determiner before a function word), so false positives stay near zero. The correction is applied retroactively (the previous word is fixed once the next word lands). Notable exclusions on purpose: 'were'->'we're' (past-tense 'were going/here/not' is valid), 'well'->'we'll' (interjection/adverb 'well' is too common), and 'go'/'loose'/'out' from 'lets' ('he lets go of' is valid). Extend by adding entries; keep trigger words to their base/root form (lowercase, no apostrophes).",
